## Run the Linux CI precheck

With Docker Desktop or Docker Engine running, execute the project gate in a
clean, disposable Linux container:

```powershell
.\scripts\check-container.ps1
```

Linux and macOS can use `sh scripts/check-container.sh`. The command builds
`Dockerfile.ci`, starts the container with `--init`, and removes it after the
run. Inside the container, `python scripts/dev.py check` owns runtime-specific
quality behavior. Docker retains the local image as a build cache.

This precheck catches clean-environment and Linux-only problems locally. GitHub
Actions still owns the Windows job and the final hosted-runner result.
